# CLAUDE.md

Workspace for Workato development with `{{REPO_DIR}}` (reusable tooling and skills).

## Layout

| Folder | What it is |
|---|---|
| `{{REPO_DIR}}/` | Tooling and skills: a separate repo (clone or submodule). Never put customer material in it. |
| `Workspace Projects/` | Hydrated Workato projects (a `wk` container: `.wk/wk.toml` plus one folder per project). Customer-specific and gitignored; never commit it. |
| `.mcp.json` | MCP config rendered by the guided setup (gitignored). Claude reads it when started from this folder. |

## Working here

- Start Claude from this folder. First run: say **start workato setup** (or `/workato-setup`).
- Run wk from `Workspace Projects/`, or use `npm run wk:pull` / `wk:status` / `wk:diff` inside `{{REPO_DIR}}/`.
- Refer to Workato assets by their UI name, with the ID in brackets only as a secondary reference.
- Add notes and docs per project in your own folders here, next to `Workspace Projects/`; keep them out of `{{REPO_DIR}}/`.
